{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n166.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"The Torah scroll is laid on the reading desk and unrolled. The reader then calls upon the Cohen, saying:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:vayaazor@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/torah/veattem@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"description","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"Before reading from the Torah, the individual called upon says the following:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:chol/shacharit/torah/barekhu@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"He then repeats this and continues:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/torah/before_blessing@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"Then the reading of the Torah begins until the end of the portion when the individual who had been called upon, says:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/torah/after_blessing@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:div","attrs":{}}
{"text":"\n          "}
{"start":"t:head","attrs":{"{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"Reading from the First Torah Scroll"}
{"end":"t:head"}
{"tail":"\n          "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"end":"t:div"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n172.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"The second scroll of the Torah is then placed next to the first on the reading desk and the Reader says half-kaddish. The first scroll is then raised and rolled together. After that, the second scroll is unrolled and someone is called to the reading for Maphtir which is taken from Pinhas."}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
